In the rural hierarchy the mezzadri were the luckier ones. Subordinate to them and much more vulnerable economically were the agricultural labourers (braccianti) without land of their own and without a contract of mezzadria; then shepherds, who lived a nomadic life shifting between pastures and markets from season to season.
